    "durationMs": 358031,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. Summary of what I built:\n\n**Stack**: Rails 8.0.2 API-only app on Ruby 3.4.3 with PostgreSQL via `DATABASE_URL` (no hard-coded credentials — the generated `database.yml` defers to the env var).\n\n**Implementation**:\n- `Link` model: validates `url` (absolute http/https with a host, stored unchanged), validates `code` format (`[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`) with uniqueness, and auto-generates unique 8-char codes when omitted (race-safe via `RecordNotUnique` retry).\n- `LinksController`: `POST /links` (201 / 409 duplicate / 422 errors), `GET /links/{code}` (200 / 404 JSON), `GET /links` (ascending creation order, `items` + `total`), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with exact `Location`, atomic single click increment).\n- Malformed JSON returns 422 via a `rescue_from ActionDispatch::Http::Parameters::ParseError` in `ApplicationController`.\n- `start.sh` runs `db:prepare` (creates DB if missing, applies pending migrations) then serves in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n- README documents startup and the API.\n\n**Notable fix**: the bundle resolved `json 3.1.0`, which breaks Rails 8.0's encoder (`unknown keyword: quirks_mode` → 500s on every render), so I pinned `json ~> 2.9`.\n\n**Verified end-to-end**: 201/409/422/404/302 paths, boundary code lengths (4 and 20 chars), empty/null code → generated, malformed/array/missing bodies, 5-way concurrent duplicate-code race (exactly one 201, rest 409), non-loopback reachability, and persistence of links and click counts across a full server restart. The links table was left empty for the test harness."
  }
